+### 2.1 Detection-contract readiness bypass
+
+Detection-contract readiness is not a UC-1/UC-2 reflection audit and MUST NOT launch this skill's normal wave machinery. The approved readiness surface is the sibling CLI command:
+
+```bash
+superclaude reflect contract-status --repo <owner/repo> --pr <number>
+superclaude reflect contract-status --validate --repo <owner/repo> --pr <number>
+```
+
+That command calls `superclaude.pr_submit.contract_setup` to diagnose readiness and optionally validate existing file-based evidence. It reports only readiness state, blockers, checked paths, hashes, counts, and the next command to run; it does not write the local lock by default, arm Monitor, mutate PR state, push, reply, resolve, retrigger, resume `/sc:pr-submit`, launch `ReflectRunner`, launch `ClaudeProcess`, or print raw GitHub payload bodies. If a user asks `/sc:sc-reflect` for detection-contract readiness, route them to the CLI command above instead of running UC-1/UC-2.
